senses.gloss:
सं-व्यान (नं) 1.
n. An upper garment;
cloth; covering.

सं-सर्ग (र्गः) 1.
m. Union, contact;
familiarity; copulation.

सं-स्कार (रः) 1.
m. Completing; puri-
fication; ceremony of purifying;
embellishment; purity; prepa-
ration; apprehension; faculty;
memory; mould.

संस्कृत (तः-ता-तं)
a. Prepared, made;
excellent; perfect; decorated;
cooked; cleansed; purified;
consecrated.
m. A regular deri-
vative; a
pandit. n. The Sans-
crit language.

सं-स्तब्ध (ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)
p. Made stiff;
stopped; corroborated.

सं-स्तम्भ (म्भः) 1.
m. Making firm;
paralysis; stop; establishing.

संस्त्याय (यः) 1.
m. Assemblage;
vicinity; diffusion; a house.

सं-स्थान (नः) 1.
m. Form; death;
fabrication, mark; heap; vicini-
ty; place where four roads meet;
spot.
a. Resembling.

सं-स्थिति (तिः) 2.
f. Death; abode;
well being; condition, duration;
contiguity; heap; restraint.

स-न्तति (तिः) 2.
f. Race, lineage;
daughter, offspring; descent;
continuous line; extent.

स-न्ताप (पः) 1.
m. Scorching heat;
affliction; repentance; passion.

सन्तापित (तः-ता-तं)
a. Scorched;
suffering from heat; inflamed.

स-न्तोष (षः) 1.
m. Joy, happiness;
thumb and forefinger.

सन्धान-करण (णं) 1.
n. Uniting;
healing; making peace.

सन्धिनी (नी) 3.
f. A cow with calf;
one milked unseasonably.

सन्ध्या (न्ध्या) 1.
f. Joining; bounda-
ry; a division or period of time;
twilight; agreement, promise;
mental combination, reflection;
name of a river and of a flower.

सन्नाह्य (ह्यः) 1.
m. A war elephant;
armoury.

सन्नि-पतित (तः-ता-तं)
a. Assembled;
blended; arrived; alighted.

सान्द्र (न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रं)
a. Thick; stout;
abundant; dense; oily; soft;
pleasing; compact.
n. A thicket;
a heap or cluster.
